# Component organization

For **all** UI work in this project:

## 1. New feature UI → new folder + new components

When adding a new section, flow, form, or feature surface:

- Create a **dedicated folder** for it (do not dump new files into an unrelated flat folder).
- Put that feature’s components, hooks, and styles **inside that folder**.
- Prefer `index.tsx` as the public entry; keep internals private to the folder.

```text
✅ GOOD
components/Drawer/EditMode/CreateMarkerFlow/
  index.tsx
  CreateMarkerForm.tsx
  MarkerTypeSelector.tsx

❌ BAD
components/Drawer/EditMode/
  CreateMarkerFlow.tsx
  CreateMarkerForm.tsx
  MarkerTypeSelector.tsx
  (and more unrelated files mixed at the same level)
```

Examples of feature folders: `EditMode/`, `ViewMode/`, `CollapseView/`, or a subfolder under them for a flow (`NewCategory/`, `CreateMarkerFlow/`).

## 2. Reusable UI → shared folder; always reuse

If a component is (or becomes) reusable across sections/features:

- Move it to a **shared** location and import it from there.
- **Do not** copy-paste markup or parallel “almost the same” components.

Shared locations (pick the narrowest that fits):

| Scope | Location |
|-------|----------|
| Drawer-wide | `src/components/Drawer/shared/` |
| App-wide | `src/components/shared/` (or an existing top-level shared component folder) |

Already-shared drawer primitives (buttons, fields, chips, headers, form shell, etc.) must be **reused**, not reimplemented.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — duplicate action button styles/markup in a new form
<button className="places-edit-action is-cancel">Cancel</button>

// ✅ GOOD — reuse shared primitive
import { DrawerActionButton } from '../shared/DrawerActionButton'
<DrawerActionButton variant="cancel">Cancel</DrawerActionButton>
```

## 3. When touching existing code

- If you introduce a second copy of the same UI pattern, **extract to shared** and update call sites in the same change.
- If a file grows into a multi-piece feature, **split it into its own folder** rather than leaving siblings scattered.
- Prefer extending an existing shared component over adding a one-off class that duplicates it.
